    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Taylor Ward** (71.18) and **Daulton Varsho** (68.79) stand out as our most potent assets. **Taylor Ward** benefits immensely from a favorable encounter with Zack Littell, bolstered by a significant park factor and a high-leverage spot at the top of the order that maximizes his scoring ceiling. Similarly, **Daulton Varsho** is a top-tier play; beyond his excellent park and platoon advantage, his efficiency is boosted by the presence of a pitcher with a slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for him to chase that scarce stolen base category we are currently prioritizing. **Jonathan Aranda** (68.94) rounds out the top trio, benefiting from a +19% SP skill adjustment against Merrill Kelly and a strong xwOBA that suggests he is undervalued by the base projections.\n\nThe decision to bench **Jung Hoo Lee** (39.08) was the most difficult call of the day, as he narrowly missed the cut behind **Tyler Freeman** (58.56). While **Jung Hoo Lee** is a steady presence, he faces a daunting matchup against Chris Sale, whose elite status forces a significant downward adjustment to his expectation; the optimizer ultimately favored the superior matchup profile of **Tyler Freeman** and the volume efficiency of our starting outfield. Managers should maintain vigilance regarding the 31% rain risk affecting both **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Taylor Ward**. While both are strong plays, the weather creates a volatile floor that could lead to an early exit or a complete washout, particularly for **Jeremiah Jackson**, who is already battling a lower-order lineup assignment. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** still sidelined on the IL, we are relying on our depth to navigate these platoon disadvantages against arms like Chris Sale.",
